# Documentation verification

The rebased issue branch retains and composes the user-facing documentation for
both features:

- `docs/run.md` documents optional producer session evidence, stage-log capture,
  digest-bound prior-attempt rerun inputs, the no-session state, resumed-session
  non-replayability, entry-reserved roles, caller-workspace provenance, and
  `read_checkout` behavior.
- `docs/gates.md` documents the prior-attempt index and evidence roles, killing
  verdict, transcript failure behavior, per-seat original-SHA checkout isolation,
  and manifest version behavior.
- `docs/replay.md` states replay uses the run's original Git SHA, documents the
  session sidecar and captured log contract, and explains recorded transcript
  handling.
- `docs/plans/product/V1-SCOPE.md` reflects the delivered issue scope without
  presenting unimplemented plans as shipped behavior.

The conflict resolution deliberately describes manifest v4 as one capability
level used when either caller provenance or stage logs appear. Caller runs require
`original_git_sha`; log-only v4 runs do not; combined runs carry both in one v4
document. The broader choice between writer-version and feature-bit semantics is
left to the already-filed issue #24.

Observed documentation checks on this tree:

```text
$ make docs-check
generated 26 command docs into /var/folders/.../tmp...

$ make docs-reality
docs-reality: OK — 16 commands; docs match the shipped CLI.
```

No new user-facing behavior was introduced by the integration-only regression
test, so no additional documentation file is required beyond preserving the
composed descriptions above.
